<title>USA: Ocean City, Md., Coke deal raises protest -- paper.</title>
<headline>Ocean City, Md., Coke deal raises protest -- paper.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>A $1.1 million deal making Coke the official soft drink of Ocean City, Md., has sparked protest among some local officials, the Washington Post reported Thursday.</p>
<p>The city's mayor, James Mathias, said the deal would help balance the city's budget, but opponents argued it was overly commercial.</p>
<p>Under the deal, Coke would be the exclusive soft drink at all city-sponsored functions and would be served in municipal buildings.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
